  "description": "<p>Quoting section 5.7.2</p>\n<blockquote><p>In addition to requirements in <a href=\"https://fedora.info/2018/06/25/spec/#append-ldprs\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">5.7.1 LDP-RS</a>, when a client is allowed to perform <tt>acl:Append</tt> but not <tt>acl:Write</tt> operations on an <a href=\"https://fedora.info/2018/06/25/spec/#dfn-ldpc\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">LDPC</a>, a <tt>POST</tt> request <em>MUST</em> be allowed. </p></blockquote>\n<p>So if you can acl:Append a LDP-C you can't PUT or PATCH or DELETE, but you can POST to add a new resource inside it.</p>",
